# Build-time values, committed on purpose.
#
# Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined by Next during `next build` and ships inside
# the JavaScript, so none of it is secret — the WhatsApp number and the origin
# are already readable in the bundle by anyone who opens the site.
#
# They used to live only as vars on the Cloudflare worker, where two things were
# wrong with them: Next never reads a runtime var for an inlined value, and a
# deploy overwrites the worker's remote configuration, which is how they were
# silently lost. Keeping them here makes every build — local, CI, anyone's
# checkout — produce the same site with no dashboard state to go missing.
#
# Secrets do NOT belong here. TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID are set
# with `wrangler secret put` and read at runtime.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.ylala.art
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=+34614272956
